    "objective chain",
    "herds with flee behaviour",
    "fires as light + warmth sources",
    "HUD",
    "pooled particle FX"
  ],
  "engineNotes": {
    "notes": [
      "3D kit: kenney_nature_kit. All 329 models are OBJs with flat materials and no textures; Meshes.loadObj ignores mtllib/usemtl and normalises every model to a unit cube centred on its origin, so each object here is scaled to its intended size and placed at y = size / 2 to stand on the ground.",
      "One colour per mesh object, by design: each tint is the face-dominant material of that model read out of the pack's own .mtl files (see tools/biggames/nature.py). Canopied trees therefore render with a green trunk -- the canopy is 2-4x the trunk's faces -- so they are used as a back-lit belt at the valley edge; the near ground uses the kit's shrubs, logs and standing stones, which read cleanly in one colour.",
      "The ranger's gravity is script-owned rather than Rigidbody3D: the terrain is a flat plane with a script-clamped boundary, and a script-owned arc behaves identically in the engine and in the offline harness (tools/run_games.js), which is where the game is tested.",
      "The sun, the sky gradient and the fog colours are driven from Valley.js through the Light and Camera3D APIs, so the day/night cycle is real lighting rather than a screen tint.",
      "Audio aliases: the store ships six UI sounds in kenney_ui_pack; every cue in this game is one of those six under a name that says what it means."
    ]
  },
